<title>USA: Foster Wheeler says wins $30 mln contract.</title>
<headline>Foster Wheeler says wins $30 mln contract.</headline>
<dateline>CLINTON, N.J. 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foster Wheeler Corp said Monday it was awarded a contract, valued at $30 million, to supply a 176 MWth circulating fluidized-bed boiler for the Sepap a.s. Steti pulp and paper mill in the Czech Republic.</p>
<p>The contract will be completed by Foster Wheeler Energia Oy of Finland, a subsidiary of Foster Wheeler's Foster Wheeler Energy International Inc.</p>
<p>The project includes delivery of new or modernized pressure parts, auxiliary equipment needed for CFB technology,  and electrification and instrumentation.</p>
<p>The company said it expects to complete the project in November 1998.</p>
</text>
